    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0285" n="281" xml:id="pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.711/136a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-24T19:00:00-05:00">February 24, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. 1. Please repeat to the Embassy at Tokyo the message quoted below, as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Reference Shanghai’s 305, February 23, 7 p.m. The Department desires
                            that you inform the Japanese Foreign Office that you are advised that
                            the Japanese military authorities are planning to impose a censorship of
                            mail at Shanghai. You should say that the censorship of American mail by
                            Japanese censors at Shanghai would be an unwarranted infringement of the
                            rights of the American nationals concerned and request that instructions
                            be sent to the appropriate Japanese authorities at Shanghai to refrain
                            from such censorship.</p>
                        <p>You may, before approaching the Foreign Office, wish to consult with your
                            interested colleagues in regard to similar but separate action by
                            them.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. The Department leaves to your discretion the question whether you should take
                    similar action at Shanghai.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d360-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d360-f1" n="69" xml:id="d360-f1-content">
                <p>Representations were made at both Tokyo and Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
